WEBVTT

00:02.048 --> 00:03.925
<i>Previously on</i> Lost:

00:03.967 --> 00:05.760
- Who are you?
- Daniel Faraday.

00:05.802 --> 00:07.210
I'm here to rescue you.

00:09.306 --> 00:12.090
I just almost died
jumping out of a helicopter

00:12.142 --> 00:14.811
- because you called us for help.
- She's lying.

00:14.853 --> 00:16.928
Whatever they came for, it isn't us.

00:16.980 --> 00:19.097
Is that from your chopper?

00:19.190 --> 00:22.767
Yeah. That...
Yeah, they reduce the weight load.

00:22.819 --> 00:25.019
What's this for?

00:25.071 --> 00:26.979
Rescuing you and your people...

00:27.032 --> 00:30.285
...I can't really say
it's our primary objective.

00:30.327 --> 00:32.120
Then what is?

00:54.434 --> 00:56.759
Hello. I'm sorry I'm late.

00:56.811 --> 00:59.095
- You must be Dr Burke.
- Juliet.

00:59.189 --> 01:02.108
Juliet. I'm Harper Stanhope.

01:02.150 --> 01:04.308
Please sit.

01:06.321 --> 01:08.146
Today is just a meet and greet

01:08.198 --> 01:10.231
so that we can get to know each other.

01:10.283 --> 01:14.444
Please don't take this the wrong way,
but I really don't think I need therapy.

01:16.039 --> 01:18.959
How about we call it "talking"
instead of therapy?

01:21.336 --> 01:22.879
- OK.
- Good.

01:22.921 --> 01:25.079
Let's talk.

01:25.799 --> 01:28.082
So you've been here a week...

01:28.969 --> 01:31.919
...and what's
your least favourite part so far?

01:32.722 --> 01:35.298
I don't like being treated
like a celebrity.

01:35.392 --> 01:37.383
And is that surprising?

01:37.477 --> 01:41.137
- You're big news right now.
- Yes, I know.

01:42.691 --> 01:45.558
I guess I don't like being
the centre of attention.

01:46.695 --> 01:48.571
It makes me feel isolated.

01:50.490 --> 01:51.773
Alone.

01:54.744 --> 01:58.488
Well, maybe you feel
that all eyes are on you...

01:59.332 --> 02:01.532
...but you're not a celebrity.

02:01.584 --> 02:05.797
And soon enough you'll realise that
you're no different than anyone here.

02:05.839 --> 02:09.499
- I know. I never meant that I...
- Yes?

02:09.592 --> 02:11.918
Harper, I'm sorry for the interruption.

02:11.970 --> 02:15.922
I know you don't like me busting in,
but Ben would like to see the doc.

02:18.810 --> 02:20.770
She's all yours, Tom.

02:23.481 --> 02:26.057
It was nice talking to you, Juliet.

02:26.151 --> 02:28.226
Welcome to the island.

02:31.448 --> 02:33.241
Harper's a real piece of work.

02:33.283 --> 02:37.026
But if you give her a week, she'll
have you crying about your daddy.

02:37.078 --> 02:39.831
I'm speaking
from personal experience here.

02:44.294 --> 02:46.494
Welcome to your humble abode.

02:48.256 --> 02:49.747
This is for me?

02:50.467 --> 02:52.010
The whole house?

02:52.052 --> 02:55.795
You're here to help us with some
very important research, Juliet.

02:55.847 --> 02:57.964
We pulled out all the stops.

02:59.809 --> 03:02.176
Two bedrooms, two baths,
washer, dryer.

03:03.021 --> 03:05.888
Fresh linens, a well-stocked fridge.

03:05.982 --> 03:09.642
And I know you love the opera.
We have all the classics on CD.

03:11.071 --> 03:12.781
Ben, this is amazing.

03:12.822 --> 03:15.940
Seriously, you shouldn't have gone
to all the trouble.

03:15.992 --> 03:18.109
I'm only gonna be here for six months.

03:18.161 --> 03:19.704
Right, of course, but...

03:21.790 --> 03:23.823
...we want you to feel at home.

03:31.883 --> 03:33.958
Need some help?

03:34.010 --> 03:37.347
I'm fine. I just can't seem
to get it steady.

03:39.140 --> 03:40.798
OK.

03:41.601 --> 03:43.561
Nice. Thanks.

03:44.354 --> 03:48.650
Why are you going to all this trouble
when we're about to leave this island?

03:48.692 --> 03:51.100
We still need somewhere
to sleep tonight.

03:51.152 --> 03:54.270
Juliet, have you seen
Charlotte and Faraday?

03:54.322 --> 03:56.647
- All their stuff's gone.
- No, I haven't.

03:56.741 --> 03:59.192
You have the sat-phone, right?

04:00.996 --> 04:03.363
He saw them going into the jungle.

04:06.042 --> 04:08.034
Why didn't he say anything?

04:11.756 --> 04:14.509
You said they are friends.

04:18.847 --> 04:20.171
Aren't they?

04:22.267 --> 04:25.760
We got a lot of ground to cover,
so let's fan out.

04:25.812 --> 04:29.597
If you cut their trail,
call out to me, I'll come to you.

05:07.103 --> 05:08.980
Jack?

05:10.774 --> 05:12.932
Hello, Juliet.

05:12.984 --> 05:14.861
Long time, no see.

05:38.218 --> 05:39.761
What are you doing here?

05:39.803 --> 05:43.713
I came to deliver a message...
from Ben.

05:44.432 --> 05:47.925
The two people you're looking for,
Faraday and Lewis,

05:47.978 --> 05:49.886
they're headed to the Tempest.

05:50.438 --> 05:53.139
And if they figure out
how to deploy that gas...

05:54.067 --> 05:58.394
...then everyone on this island
is going to die.

06:00.782 --> 06:04.035
- Why don't you stop them?
- Because Ben wants you to go.

06:04.077 --> 06:07.570
How can Ben know where they are
when he's a prisoner?

06:07.622 --> 06:10.323
Ben is exactly where he wants to be.

06:18.091 --> 06:21.344
- How am I supposed to stop them?
- By pointing the gun

06:21.386 --> 06:23.961
and pulling the trigger.

06:24.014 --> 06:25.171
Hey!

06:27.767 --> 06:29.926
Who are you?

06:31.187 --> 06:33.221
I'm an old friend of Juliet's.

06:34.899 --> 06:38.476
I just told her where the people
you're looking for are headed.

06:38.528 --> 06:41.020
Maybe you and your gun can go too.

07:25.450 --> 07:27.160
You OK?

07:28.787 --> 07:32.739
I was just looking for some gauze.
I didn't know anyone was here.

07:39.005 --> 07:40.913
How'd you manage that?

07:41.007 --> 07:44.542
I... I work over at the power station.

07:44.594 --> 07:46.878
I pressed up against a transformer.

07:48.556 --> 07:51.007
Take a seat.
Let me take a look at it.

07:59.567 --> 08:01.476
You're Burke, right?

08:02.153 --> 08:03.561
The baby doctor.

08:05.824 --> 08:07.899
What gave me away?

08:10.537 --> 08:12.862
I heard we lost Henrietta this morning.

08:15.208 --> 08:17.085
It's OK. It's not your fault.

08:17.127 --> 08:19.577
Pregnant women
are dying on this island.

08:21.423 --> 08:23.873
I was brought here to help fix that.

08:25.260 --> 08:27.220
So whose fault is it?

08:28.054 --> 08:31.839
Believe me, no one expects you
to fix it overnight.

08:36.479 --> 08:39.347
You have anyone to talk to?
Any friends here?

08:42.527 --> 08:45.614
- Maybe Harper.
- Harper hates me.

08:45.655 --> 08:47.897
We only talk because we have to.

08:47.949 --> 08:52.360
I get the feeling that she's a mean
and spiteful person.

08:55.332 --> 08:57.365
She's my wife.

08:59.127 --> 09:00.587
She's your wife?

09:03.131 --> 09:06.624
- I'm sorry.
- No, don't worry about it. It's OK.

09:06.676 --> 09:09.001
OK, you're... you're set.

09:11.640 --> 09:13.381
Much obliged, ma'am.

09:16.561 --> 09:20.221
Hey, I know this place can wear on you,

09:20.273 --> 09:22.150
but if you need to talk...

09:23.360 --> 09:25.070
...l'm around.

09:25.111 --> 09:26.352
Good to know.

09:27.280 --> 09:32.984
Oh, if you promise not to tell your wife
what I said about her...

09:33.828 --> 09:37.530
...I won't tell anyone you lied
about how you hurt your arm.

09:39.960 --> 09:42.660
I know a chemical burn when I see one.

09:47.926 --> 09:49.834
You got a deal.

09:54.015 --> 09:56.090
By the way...

09:58.019 --> 09:59.677
...l'm Goodwin.

10:00.313 --> 10:02.023
Juliet.

10:12.409 --> 10:15.412
Faraday and Charlotte
are heading for the Tempest.

10:15.453 --> 10:18.707
- The Tempest?
- It's safer if I don't talk about it.

10:18.748 --> 10:20.375
No, talk about it, please.

10:20.417 --> 10:23.336
It's an electrical station
that powers the island.

10:23.378 --> 10:25.286
Why would they go there?

10:28.550 --> 10:31.219
If there's something
you need to tell me...

10:31.261 --> 10:33.054
...now's the time to do it.

10:35.598 --> 10:37.715
What I need is for you to help me.

10:37.809 --> 10:39.550
Will you help me?

10:46.609 --> 10:50.269
If we move all night,
maybe we can still catch them.

10:54.284 --> 10:55.358
Thank you.

11:05.462 --> 11:07.495
I think it's that way.

11:11.718 --> 11:14.502
What happens if I...

11:16.681 --> 11:18.589
What if I can't do it?

11:19.851 --> 11:21.394
Dan.

11:22.312 --> 11:23.803
Look at me.

11:25.774 --> 11:28.443
I know you can do this.

11:31.446 --> 11:33.156
We should get going.

11:36.242 --> 11:37.953
Yeah.

11:38.453 --> 11:39.777
Come on.

11:43.917 --> 11:46.325
It's OK. It's OK. It's Kate.

11:56.805 --> 11:58.181
So they have Miles?

11:59.849 --> 12:03.186
Yeah, but he's fine.
They're treating him fine.

12:03.770 --> 12:06.304
I thought you two
were with Jack at the beach.

12:08.108 --> 12:10.099
What are you guys doing out here?

12:11.403 --> 12:14.656
Jack was trying to communicate
with Sayid and Desmond,

12:14.698 --> 12:17.648
but the sat-phone ran out of juice.

12:17.701 --> 12:21.152
It's totally dead.
There's no way we can call the boat.

12:21.997 --> 12:26.626
So we volunteered to get spare batteries
out the packs we threw out the chopper.

12:28.336 --> 12:32.382
So if you threw your pack
from the chopper,

12:32.424 --> 12:33.498
what's that?

12:35.385 --> 12:39.045
This... I just borrowed this.

12:40.932 --> 12:43.007
Mind if I take a look?

12:46.438 --> 12:48.096
Go ahead, Dan, show her.

12:56.656 --> 12:57.772
Batteries, huh?

12:57.866 --> 12:59.659
What's this...?

13:04.039 --> 13:05.279
What?

13:12.547 --> 13:15.164
- That woman, what was her name?
- Harper.

13:16.009 --> 13:19.262
- The two of you friends?
- Not exactly.

13:19.304 --> 13:22.672
- She was my therapist.
- You people had therapists?

13:22.724 --> 13:26.175
It's very stressful
being an Other, Jack.

13:28.396 --> 13:32.557
- Seemed hostile, even for a therapist.
- There are things from your past

13:32.609 --> 13:36.821
- you'd rather not talk about.
- Yeah. You read them all in my file.

13:38.281 --> 13:40.951
Trust me, Jack,
you don't want to see my file.

13:45.538 --> 13:48.906
The problem occurs somewhere
during the second trimester

13:48.959 --> 13:51.628
when the mother's immune system
is triggered.

13:51.670 --> 13:53.995
The white blood cell count plummets.

13:54.089 --> 13:57.957
It's like the immune system
turns on the foetus.

13:59.511 --> 14:01.335
- May I?
- Sure.

14:07.936 --> 14:11.679
- Any thought yet on a cause?
- It's really too early to tell,

14:11.731 --> 14:16.142
but only women who have conceived
on the island does it happen to which...

14:16.194 --> 14:18.019
Hey, Juliet.

14:21.199 --> 14:23.076
Ben, I didn't know you were here.

14:24.619 --> 14:27.820
Ethan's out sick.
I have an extra egg salad on rye.

14:27.872 --> 14:30.281
I was just checking if Juliet wants it.

14:30.333 --> 14:32.127
Thanks. I already ate.

14:32.168 --> 14:35.088
I have an appointment
with your wife in ten minutes.

14:35.130 --> 14:37.830
Great. Tell her I said hi.

14:39.050 --> 14:40.760
Oh, will do.

14:42.012 --> 14:44.462
- Ben?
- No, I'm fine.

14:59.487 --> 15:03.064
So, Juliet, what do you think of Ben?

15:05.201 --> 15:07.276
He's great.

15:08.121 --> 15:11.072
Very smart and intense.

15:11.124 --> 15:13.199
Challenging.

15:13.877 --> 15:16.744
- He's been really good to me.
- Of course he has.

15:16.796 --> 15:18.830
You look just like her.

15:19.883 --> 15:21.124
I'm sorry?

15:21.176 --> 15:23.876
I see you and my husband
have become friendly.

15:27.849 --> 15:30.717
Yeah. He's great.

15:31.603 --> 15:33.720
He's been really helpful.

15:36.900 --> 15:39.600
When did you start sleeping with him?

15:40.904 --> 15:42.645
What?

15:44.366 --> 15:48.067
Look, Juliet, I'm not an idiot,
so just tell me.

15:48.161 --> 15:50.121
When did it start?

15:51.957 --> 15:55.241
OK, I'm not doing this. We're done.

15:55.293 --> 15:58.327
No, please respect me enough
to spare me the pretence

15:58.421 --> 16:00.538
that you are actually offended.

16:00.590 --> 16:03.958
I know. I followed you.

16:06.930 --> 16:09.172
Watched you.

16:16.773 --> 16:19.265
- I'm sorry.
- It doesn't matter anymore.

16:19.317 --> 16:21.194
But what does matter

16:21.278 --> 16:24.562
is that you listen to me
and that you believe me.

16:27.492 --> 16:32.653
Now if you continue to have
a relationship with Goodwin...

16:33.748 --> 16:35.782
...there will be consequences.

16:37.669 --> 16:41.746
- I don't want him to get hurt.
- I would never hurt him.

16:41.798 --> 16:43.915
I am not talking about you.

16:43.967 --> 16:46.751
I am talking about Ben.

16:54.185 --> 16:56.427
Hi, John.

16:56.521 --> 16:58.231
Hey, Claire.

17:01.860 --> 17:03.851
Is there something I can do for you?

17:03.903 --> 17:06.270
I want to know
what's going on with Miles.

17:06.406 --> 17:08.147
Right now not a whole lot.

17:08.199 --> 17:12.495
I'm bringing him food and water
until he decides to talk.

17:13.997 --> 17:16.531
I'd like to talk to him myself.

17:17.459 --> 17:19.283
Why would you want to do that?

17:19.336 --> 17:21.953
John, we have to find out
who these people are

17:22.005 --> 17:26.082
and where they came from... and why
they're not interested in rescuing us.

17:26.134 --> 17:29.085
- You don't think I'll get that?
- No, I...

17:30.805 --> 17:33.808
I just think we might be
taking the wrong approach.

17:33.850 --> 17:37.103
I mean, you killed one,
Ben shot one.

17:37.187 --> 17:39.429
Now we're holding one prisoner.

17:39.522 --> 17:43.683
You know, it's not hard to understand
why they might think we're hostile.

17:45.987 --> 17:48.479
I might be just
a little less intimidating.

17:50.408 --> 17:52.775
- It's not going to happen, Claire.
- John.

17:52.869 --> 17:55.820
You do remember what Charlie said
about these people.

17:55.914 --> 17:58.698
All Charlie said
was whose boat it isn't.

18:00.168 --> 18:03.578
Don't you want to know whose boat it is?

18:24.442 --> 18:27.935
- Rabbit today?
- We're running out of chickens.

18:31.199 --> 18:34.202
This didn't have a number on it, did it?

18:34.286 --> 18:36.319
What?

18:36.371 --> 18:39.322
Eat, change. Put your laundry
and dishes by the door.

18:39.374 --> 18:41.741
I'll be back to collect them
in 15 minutes.

18:41.793 --> 18:44.410
So has the revolution begun yet?

18:50.302 --> 18:52.043
What are you talking about?

18:53.471 --> 18:56.808
Well, you're the leader now.
I know it's a tough position.

18:57.142 --> 19:01.094
You have to deal with all those people
second-guessing decisions.

19:01.146 --> 19:03.982
It starts out so innocently, doesn't it?

19:04.024 --> 19:08.184
A question here, a comment there.
And then if you're not careful,

19:08.278 --> 19:11.687
you find you have a full-blown
insurrection on your hands.

19:11.740 --> 19:15.817
Believe me, your people
are gonna be so angry

19:15.869 --> 19:19.237
when they realise
you still don't have a plan.

19:21.625 --> 19:23.585
And I assume you have a plan.

19:24.461 --> 19:26.369
I always have a plan.

19:26.421 --> 19:29.789
Does it involve
you raising $3.2 million?

19:33.094 --> 19:34.888
That's a lot of money.

19:35.889 --> 19:37.349
Wait.

19:38.725 --> 19:40.842
Maybe this will get you started.

19:43.396 --> 19:45.638
Put your laundry and dishes
by the door.

19:47.442 --> 19:50.695
I can help you, John.
We have shared interests.

19:51.821 --> 19:55.273
- Or at least a common enemy.
- Our friends on the freighter.

19:55.325 --> 19:59.068
Not them. The one they work for.

20:01.539 --> 20:03.740
Let me out of here.

20:04.125 --> 20:07.379
Give me some semblance of freedom.
Let me sleep in a bed,

20:07.462 --> 20:09.704
eat with utensils,
and I give you my word

20:09.756 --> 20:13.041
- I'll tell you everything...
- See, there's the problem.

20:13.093 --> 20:14.917
I don't trust your word.

20:16.513 --> 20:17.837
All right, then.

20:23.478 --> 20:26.763
I guess I'll have to show you.

20:43.581 --> 20:45.782
I hope this is good.

20:45.875 --> 20:48.962
I don't know much about wine.
I swiped this off the sub.

20:55.802 --> 20:57.377
There.

20:57.429 --> 20:59.055
Thanks.

21:07.647 --> 21:09.764
I wish we could do this all the time.

21:11.401 --> 21:15.186
I hate that we have to be so... private.

21:15.947 --> 21:18.731
What's the matter with being private?

21:18.783 --> 21:23.079
It's ridiculous. I've been sleeping
on the couch for a year.

21:23.121 --> 21:25.321
Why am I not just telling her?

21:26.791 --> 21:29.117
I don't think it's a good idea.

21:36.468 --> 21:37.542
Why not?

21:40.013 --> 21:41.640
Ben wouldn't like it.

21:41.681 --> 21:44.716
That's what this is about?
You're worried about Ben?

21:46.561 --> 21:48.720
Why, because he has a crush on you?

21:50.690 --> 21:52.974
- You know?
- Come on, everyone knows.

21:53.026 --> 21:55.184
He follows you around like a puppy.

21:56.571 --> 21:58.980
And you don't think that's a problem?

21:59.532 --> 22:03.776
A little less than a kilometre from here
he has me working with chemicals

22:03.828 --> 22:08.041
that could kill every man, woman
and child if I flipped the wrong switch.

22:09.334 --> 22:11.492
Trust me, Ben has enough on his plate.

22:11.586 --> 22:13.953
The last thing he cares about
is you and me.

22:14.756 --> 22:16.549
I just...

22:16.591 --> 22:19.083
...get the feeling
that he would be upset.

22:21.262 --> 22:23.139
What's Ben gonna do?

22:34.818 --> 22:36.778
Goodwin!

22:38.530 --> 22:41.564
- You see where the tail landed?
- Probably in the water.

22:41.616 --> 22:45.359
You can make that shore in an hour.
Ethan, get up to that fuselage.

22:45.453 --> 22:47.445
There may actually be survivors.

22:47.497 --> 22:50.667
And you're one of 'em.
A passenger. You're in shock.

22:50.709 --> 22:53.878
Come up with a story if they ask.
Stay quiet if they don't.

22:53.920 --> 22:58.498
Listen. Learn. Don't get involved.
I want lists in three days. Go.

23:17.819 --> 23:21.229
Something's wrong. We should've
caught up with them by now.

23:21.281 --> 23:23.950
These people base-jumped
out of a helicopter.

23:23.992 --> 23:26.401
Let's give them
the benefit of the doubt.

23:31.291 --> 23:33.658
Hey. Hey.

23:33.710 --> 23:35.785
It's OK. Hey. It's all right.

23:35.837 --> 23:37.120
It's OK.

23:37.172 --> 23:38.715
Hey.

23:40.383 --> 23:43.084
It's OK. You're all right. Come on.

23:44.054 --> 23:45.930
Take it easy.

23:45.972 --> 23:47.349
Take it easy.

23:50.352 --> 23:53.605
- I'll go get her some water.
- Yeah. Thanks.

23:58.526 --> 23:59.986
What happened?

24:02.072 --> 24:04.605
I was going back to the beach and...

24:05.283 --> 24:09.277
I ran into Faraday
and that woman... Charlotte.

24:09.371 --> 24:10.830
I think she hit me.

24:10.872 --> 24:14.240
They disappeared out of camp
last night. Trying to catch up.

24:17.003 --> 24:19.245
Do you know where they were headed?

24:19.297 --> 24:23.082
Some sort of... power station.

24:23.885 --> 24:25.126
Jack.

24:26.346 --> 24:28.337
They had gas masks.

24:33.103 --> 24:34.479
Juliet.

24:36.356 --> 24:37.930
Juliet!

24:45.448 --> 24:46.992
Juliet!

24:50.287 --> 24:51.746
Juliet!

25:00.255 --> 25:02.330
All right, no tricks.

25:03.717 --> 25:07.251
You're not leading me out
into the jungle so you can disappear

25:07.304 --> 25:09.973
or shoot me in the back.

25:10.015 --> 25:11.391
No tricks, John.

25:11.474 --> 25:14.008
We don't even have to leave
the living room.

25:15.895 --> 25:17.470
So let's have it.

25:18.898 --> 25:20.306
We have a deal, right?

25:21.484 --> 25:25.530
How do I know you won't run off and
meet your people first chance you get?

25:25.572 --> 25:30.316
If my people still wanted me they'd
have stormed this camp long ago.

25:34.331 --> 25:36.531
It's behind that picture.

25:50.013 --> 25:52.046
Thirty-six, 15, 28.

26:17.207 --> 26:18.750
"Red Sox"?

26:19.125 --> 26:21.284
I taped over the game.

26:49.281 --> 26:50.907
This is Charles Widmore.

26:53.493 --> 26:56.579
This is the man whose boat
is parked offshore.

26:59.833 --> 27:03.451
This is the man that's been trying
to find the island.

27:10.218 --> 27:12.043
Who's the man in the blindfold?

27:12.095 --> 27:15.265
One of my people that had
the misfortune to get caught.

27:15.307 --> 27:18.883
- How does Widmore know of the island?
- I don't know, but he does.

27:18.935 --> 27:21.552
What does he want?

27:21.604 --> 27:24.222
Three months ago
in Gainesville, Florida,

27:24.274 --> 27:27.193
the Virgin Mary seemed to appear
in a patch of mould

27:27.235 --> 27:29.394
on the side of an old housing complex.

27:29.446 --> 27:34.482
When word got out, over 5,000 people
came to see her face for themselves.

27:34.534 --> 27:37.819
You've survived an airline crash
on this island.

27:37.871 --> 27:42.083
One minute you're in a wheelchair,
the next doing jumping jacks.

27:42.125 --> 27:44.826
If 5,000 people came out
to see a piece of mould,

27:44.878 --> 27:48.162
how many people do you think
would come out to see you?

27:52.010 --> 27:54.460
Charles Widmore
wants to exploit this island.

27:54.512 --> 27:57.088
He'll do everything in his power
to possess it.

28:14.449 --> 28:18.276
Everything I know about Charles Widmore
is contained in this file.

28:18.328 --> 28:22.280
Some of it's vague, some of it's
guesswork, some of it's concrete,

28:22.332 --> 28:25.199
but this is everything,
and now it's all yours.

28:29.798 --> 28:32.415
I'm sorry I didn't tell
you all this sooner...

28:34.803 --> 28:37.587
...but it was the only
bargaining chip I had left.

28:40.266 --> 28:42.425
There's one more thing I need to know.

28:44.437 --> 28:48.765
Your man on the boat,
I want you to tell me who it is.

28:51.736 --> 28:53.478
All right.

28:54.656 --> 28:56.814
But you might want to sit down.

29:04.958 --> 29:06.949
She came through here.

29:07.711 --> 29:10.203
So did they, about
half an hour ahead of her.

29:12.799 --> 29:14.957
- What happened?
- Sorry?

29:15.010 --> 29:17.001
At Locke's. Why did you stay?

29:18.847 --> 29:21.933
I stayed because I had
to find something out.

29:21.975 --> 29:23.351
Are you gonna tell me

29:23.393 --> 29:27.439
or are we gonna keep walking through
the jungle like it doesn't matter?

29:34.738 --> 29:38.314
I stayed to find out if the people
on the freighter know who I am.

29:38.366 --> 29:40.983
If they knew that I'm a fugitive...

29:41.036 --> 29:43.069
...that I'm wanted for murder.

29:44.539 --> 29:46.572
Do they?

29:47.500 --> 29:49.461
Yeah, they know.

29:52.005 --> 29:53.663
We should keep moving.

29:53.757 --> 29:55.790
God knows where Juliet is.

30:33.922 --> 30:35.913
Hi, come on in.

30:37.092 --> 30:40.543
Sorry, have to get this ham
out of the oven, or it'll dry out.

30:40.595 --> 30:42.472
Please, don't mind me.

30:42.514 --> 30:45.517
- How are you feeling, by the way?
- Never better.

30:48.269 --> 30:49.896
Smells delicious.

30:53.650 --> 30:55.892
Ben, I thought this was a dinner party.

30:55.944 --> 30:57.226
Just you and me.

30:59.447 --> 31:01.773
I guess I should've made that clearer.

31:04.035 --> 31:07.236
No, it's fine.
I hope you like dinner rolls.

31:07.289 --> 31:09.249
I do indeed.

31:14.087 --> 31:17.955
I want to thank you for how wonderful
you've been with Zach and Emma.

31:18.049 --> 31:20.375
They're really sweet kids.

31:22.762 --> 31:27.840
Ben, they've been asking me
about their mother in Los Angeles.

31:27.892 --> 31:31.427
- I'm not really sure what to say.
- They'll stop asking in time.

31:32.188 --> 31:34.180
They're children.

31:34.232 --> 31:35.890
Do they really belong here?

31:36.735 --> 31:38.528
They're on the list, Juliet.

31:38.570 --> 31:41.906
Who are we to question
who's on the list and who's not?

31:43.783 --> 31:48.163
Now that we have everyone on the list
for the tail section what about Goodwin?

31:50.498 --> 31:52.824
He's been undercover for three weeks.

31:57.005 --> 31:59.580
He's making a case
for this woman, Ana Lucia.

32:01.092 --> 32:04.043
He thinks she'd be
a valuable member of our society.

32:04.095 --> 32:06.462
But between you and me,
I don't see it.

32:06.806 --> 32:09.757
He feels very passionately about her.

32:10.101 --> 32:12.468
Almost inappropriately so.

32:13.438 --> 32:15.398
After losing Ethan, it's a risk.

32:15.440 --> 32:18.307
Goodwin stays where he's at
right now, Juliet.

32:18.360 --> 32:22.145
There's no reason for him
to hurry back, right?

32:22.572 --> 32:26.274
But his assignment will be over soon.
I promise you.

32:31.289 --> 32:35.199
<i>Warning: computer switching</i>
<i>to manual operation.</i>

32:35.293 --> 32:37.452
<i>This attempt is unauthorised.</i>

32:50.684 --> 32:54.844
<i>Warning: manual entry.</i>
<i>Override denied.</i>

32:55.939 --> 33:00.266
<i>Warning: manual entry.</i>
<i>Override denied.</i>

33:00.318 --> 33:03.603
<i>Repeated attempts to access</i>
<i>storage tanks</i>

33:03.655 --> 33:05.813
<i>will result in contamination.</i>

33:09.202 --> 33:11.903
<i>Repeated attempts to access</i>
<i>storage tanks...</i>

33:11.997 --> 33:13.112
Hey!

33:17.085 --> 33:20.828
Juliet, what are you doing here?

33:26.428 --> 33:27.835
<i>Final warning.</i>

33:27.887 --> 33:30.380
<i>Manual override failed.</i>

33:30.432 --> 33:34.894
- Step away from the computer.
- I'm so sorry. I can't do that.

33:34.936 --> 33:38.805
<i>Manual override failed.</i>
<i>Counter-measures will begin.</i>

33:38.857 --> 33:40.765
Hey!

33:42.444 --> 33:44.811
<i>One minute to contamination.</i>

33:46.156 --> 33:49.190
Wanna release the gas?
You'll die with the rest of us.

33:49.242 --> 33:53.236
No, no. I'm not trying to release it.
I'm trying to render it inert.

33:53.288 --> 33:56.823
Juliet, I just want to make it safe.

34:00.337 --> 34:02.620
<i>Forty seconds to contamination.</i>

34:13.808 --> 34:16.478
<i>Thirty seconds to contamination.</i>

34:22.317 --> 34:25.070
<i>Warning: contamination imminent.</i>

34:25.153 --> 34:26.863
<i>Evacuate immediately.</i>

34:41.336 --> 34:43.536
<i>Twenty seconds to contamination.</i>

34:43.588 --> 34:46.122
Whatever he's doing, tell him to stop.

34:46.174 --> 34:49.542
We're trying to disable it
before he can use it against us.

34:50.303 --> 34:51.930
Juliet...

34:52.889 --> 34:55.590
...look me in the eye
and tell me you are certain

34:55.642 --> 34:59.552
Benjamin Linus wouldn't use this gas
to kill everyone on this island!

34:59.854 --> 35:01.888
We know he's used it before.

35:01.940 --> 35:04.348
If you wanna stop us,
you have to shoot us both.

35:04.401 --> 35:06.111
<i>Ten seconds to contamination.</i>

35:06.152 --> 35:08.029
- Daniel!
- Yeah, I'm trying.

35:09.698 --> 35:11.939
Come on!

35:11.992 --> 35:13.066
Come on!

35:13.118 --> 35:14.192
<i>...five...</i>

35:15.078 --> 35:16.486
<i>...four...</i>

35:17.247 --> 35:19.322
<i>...three...</i>

35:19.374 --> 35:21.199
<i>...two...</i>

35:50.530 --> 35:53.981
That... that was a close one.

36:15.513 --> 36:17.880
- What are you reading?
- Shephard's file.

36:17.932 --> 36:19.559
Mikhail dropped it off.

36:22.103 --> 36:24.303
He's a spinal surgeon, Ben.

36:24.356 --> 36:27.359
He has extensive experience
in tumour removal.

36:30.820 --> 36:32.937
- How about that?
- He can help you.

36:39.829 --> 36:43.573
I thought you'd be more excited.
What's wrong?

36:47.420 --> 36:49.454
I need you to come with me.

36:55.679 --> 37:00.381
After out last raid on the tail-section
survivors, they ran off, left the beach.

37:01.935 --> 37:06.231
I sent Pickett and Tom to track
their location. They came across this.

37:07.148 --> 37:08.973
I'm sorry, Juliet.

37:09.025 --> 37:11.059
Sorry about what?

37:13.822 --> 37:15.813
Oh, my God.

37:16.449 --> 37:18.243
Oh, my God.

37:18.285 --> 37:21.037
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

37:22.664 --> 37:23.946
Oh, my God!

37:26.960 --> 37:28.618
Goodwin.

37:31.256 --> 37:32.632
What happened?

37:33.758 --> 37:36.626
We don't know.
There weren't any witnesses.

37:36.720 --> 37:40.004
I can only assume they found out
he wasn't one of them.

37:41.850 --> 37:45.760
- Guess I should've listened to you.
- Why are you showing me this?

37:49.733 --> 37:52.183
Why did you bring me out here?

37:52.694 --> 37:55.311
What, you mean instead of his wife?

38:01.494 --> 38:03.695
You knew this would happen.

38:06.833 --> 38:10.368
You sent him out here because
you knew this would happen.

38:11.004 --> 38:14.789
You wanted this.
You wanted him to die!

38:16.843 --> 38:18.042
Why?

38:19.012 --> 38:21.087
Why?

38:22.682 --> 38:24.924
You're asking me why?

38:25.685 --> 38:30.148
After everything I did to get you here,
everything I've done to keep you here,

38:30.190 --> 38:32.724
how can you possibly not understand...

38:34.694 --> 38:36.728
...that you're mine?

38:44.621 --> 38:46.414
Take as much time as you need.

39:11.231 --> 39:14.015
Kate, it's all right.
They're on our side.

39:14.067 --> 39:17.810
"Our side", Juliet?
She just knocked me unconscious.

39:18.280 --> 39:21.397
Yeah. I'm very sorry about that,
but I had no choice!

39:24.035 --> 39:27.038
Look, Daniel's inside
securing the facility.

39:27.080 --> 39:30.114
If you come with me,
I'll be more than happy to explain

39:30.166 --> 39:32.408
exactly how we just saved your life!

39:36.298 --> 39:38.289
All right, let's go.

39:42.095 --> 39:44.128
I'll take their word for it.

39:52.856 --> 39:54.597
You OK?

39:59.154 --> 40:01.145
He wanted me to kill them.

40:04.242 --> 40:06.526
Ben. He told me to kill both of them.

40:12.042 --> 40:15.326
- How can he tell you anything?
- I don't know.

40:15.378 --> 40:19.706
But he knew how to get to me, knew where
they were going, what they were doing.

40:19.758 --> 40:21.635
Don't you understand?

40:21.676 --> 40:25.044
These people came here
to wage war against Ben.

40:26.056 --> 40:29.424
And Ben's gonna win, Jack.

40:29.476 --> 40:32.562
And when he does, you don't
want to be anywhere near me.

40:34.230 --> 40:35.607
Why not?

40:39.110 --> 40:41.269
Because he thinks that I'm his.

40:44.074 --> 40:46.649
And he knows how I feel about you.

41:10.016 --> 41:12.216
He knows where to find me.

41:34.291 --> 41:35.573
Beat that.

41:45.343 --> 41:47.220
Son of a bitch!

41:48.972 --> 41:51.339
How'd you get so damn good
at horseshoes?

41:51.433 --> 41:53.716
I don't know. Guess I'm just lucky.

42:01.443 --> 42:03.768
What the hell are you doing out?

42:04.696 --> 42:06.020
See you guys at dinner.
